<% content_for :title, 'Allegiances' %>

<%= render 'help/page', title: 'Allegiances' do %>
  <div class='space-y-8'>

    <p class='text-fg-muted'>
      Allegiances identify the political entities — empires, consulates, federations, and the
      like — that star systems and worlds owe fealty to. A system and its worlds are assigned an
      allegiance independently, so a border system can carry worlds loyal to different powers.
    </p>

    <div>
      <dl class='space-y-6'>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Code</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            The allegiance's short identifying code, as used on the starmap and in UWP data
            (e.g. <span class='font-mono text-fg-bright'>3eIm</span> for the Third Imperium).
            Must be unique.
          </dd>
        </div>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Name</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            The allegiance's full display name.
          </dd>
        </div>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Legacy Code</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            An older or alternate code carried over from imported data, kept for reference
            alongside the current code.
          </dd>
        </div>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Colour</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Background and border colours used to render the allegiance's territory on the
            starmap.
          </dd>
        </div>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Statistics</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Statistics are calculated from all star systems that owe fealty to this allegiance.
          </dd>
        </div>

      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class='pt-2 text-right uppercase font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.22em] text-fg-muted'>
      REFERENCE 0819AL
    </div>

  </div>
<% end %>
